  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppCare 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'Although your mother is responding well to the new treatment, managing
    side effects at home and coordinating follow-up care has been challenging. You
    share these concerns through a caregiver survey.


    <b>How can caregiver feedback
    like this contribute to post-market surveillance for newly approved treatments?</b>'
  explanation: "When caregivers share real-life challenges\u2014like managing side
    effects at home or coordinating follow-up care\u2014this information helps researchers
    and healthcare teams see where support may be lacking after a treatment is approved.
    As part of post-market surveillance, this feedback can lead to better education,
    closer monitoring, and improved care resources to help future patients and families
    manage treatment more safely and confidently."
  correctAnswer: It helps identify gaps in support and guides improvements in patient
    education, monitoring, and care resources.
  incorrectAnswer1: It gives caregivers permission to adjust treatment plans without
    involving the healthcare team.
  incorrectAnswer2: 'It replaces the need for ongoing safety monitoring once a new
    treatment is approved. '
  incorrectAnswer3: It guarantees that future patients will not experience side effects
    from the new treatment.
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Approval
